# What `scripts/package_linux.sh` writes. The archive is 14 MB and is rebuilt
# from a commit by a script — putting it in git would be storing the output of
# a function beside the function.
dist/
__pycache__/

# The name bank's tier 3 — every spelling one single city register ever used.
#
# 60,548 rows, 13.1 MB, and nothing loads them: `include_str!` carries only the
# bank itself, and tier 3 exists so the next task does not have to download
# four cities again. `scripts/build_de_names.py --fetch` writes it beside the
# bank; git does not carry it, and the gate compares the bank alone.
z_core/assets/de_names_v2_tier3.csv
